From: SOAR Lab <local>
Date: 2026-11-08
Subject: worker: async swarm dispatch after durable result merge

In swarm mode, handleWorkflowQueue (the /api/v1/streams handler) ran
ValidateFinished + handleExecutionResult (full decide + child dispatch
+ backend sendResult) synchronously BEFORE writing the HTTP response.
Under parallel fanout each app-side send_result POST waited seconds for
the transaction, exceeding the app SDK 10s read timeout - producing
Read timeouts, retry storms and duplicate action deliveries around
every dependency hop.

The result is already durable at that point (setWorkflowExecution ran,
cache + backend updated). Move the decide/dispatch block to a goroutine
so the POST returns immediately after the merge; children still get
dispatched from current cached state inside handleExecutionResult.
Scope: the block is already gated by SHUFFLE_SWARM_CONFIG == run|swarm,
so Docker-mode semantics are unchanged. Duplicate dispatches are still
deduped by the existing "result already found (PRE REQUEST)" checks.

